      "text": "Over \"9,500\" miles away, the U.S. fought Japan during WWII; also over \"9,500\" miles away, the U.S. fought aggression in Korea and Vietnam; today, over \"9,500\" miles away in East Asia, the U.S. maintains its largest overseas military deployment, more than half of its global total, and its largest Combatant Command with the most concentrated fire power in the world led by the most capable military leaders, with most mutual defense partners (esp. Japan, ROK, the Philippines and Australia), all for the specific purpose of deterring, and fighting against, another imperialist and communist aggression and keeping peace through strength.\n\nJust saying...",
