      "text": "A dog named Haven has become an internet sensation after miraculously finding his way home two weeks after being swept away by floodwaters during Typhoon Tino in the Philippines.\n\nOn November 4, 2025, powerful floods struck Villa del Rio in Barangay Bacayan, Cebu City. Owner Emmanuel Llenos was forced to prioritize rescuing his family and smaller pets, leaving Haven behind in the chaos. Despite extensive searches and appeals on social media, there was no sign of the dog.\n\nThe family eventually relocated due to severe flood damage but continued returning to their old home in hopes of a miracle. That miracle arrived when Haven suddenly reappeared — exhausted, covered in mud, but alive. He had found his way back to the exact spot where he was last seen.\n\nEmmanuel described the emotional reunion as overwhelming joy. He also called it “good karma,” recalling how he had rescued a woman stranded on an electric post during the height of the flooding.",
