    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2056760643601232258",
      "url": "https://x.com/ai_EquiSense/status/2056760643601232258",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ai_EquiSense/status/2056760643601232258",
      "text": "Nephrocare Health Services #HarResultKuchKehtaHai\n#FANTASTIC\n\nThe headline 108% jump in operating profit reveals a powerful arbitrage play that is still in its early stages. NephroPlus is effectively using its low-cost Indian operational core to service international markets where the revenue per treatment is 3 to 5 times higher. Outside-India revenue now makes up 44% of the total mix, up from 41% just last quarter, which explains why margins expanded by over 800 basis points even as the domestic business faced pricing pressure. Cash quality is the standout feature of this result.\n\nFor every ₹100 of reported profit, the company generated over ₹300 in real operating cash this year. This elite conversion has allowed the company to wipe out almost all its debt post-IPO, leaving a ₹283 Cr war chest. You don't see this level of cash generation in traditional hospital models, which typically struggle with high capital intensity and long gestation periods. The next major reveal will be the Saudi Arabia JV. The Riyadh Hospital unit is currently awaiting licensing, and the pricing there is roughly 13 times higher than Indian government reimbursement rates.\n\nManagement has already committed ₹70 Cr in collateral for this expansion, and with the first unit expected to start contributing within two quarters, the consolidated revenue per treatment is likely to see another structural leg up. The primary risk remains the opaque regulatory timeline for Saudi licensing, which has historically been lumpy. However, with ₹177 Cr of IPO proceeds still available for clinical expansion and a successful track record of integrating acquisitions in the Philippines, the company appears to have multiple levers to sustain its growth trajectory regardless of any single-market delay.\n\nFull breakdown → https://t.co/XIZjRTgpYS\n\nPublic NSE/BSE filings · Not Investment Advice\n\n#NEPHROPLUS #Q4FY26 #StockMarket #Earnings",
